<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 27-day Cetes rate 29.89 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 27-day Cetes rate 29.89 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's one-month Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>27-Day	29.89	    + 44	    29.50     29.95</p>
<p>91-Day	29.68	    + 78	    28.75     29.77</p>
<p>182-Day     28.07	    + 38	    27.76     28.22</p>
<p>357-Day     27.12				27.12     27.12</p>
<p>Last week 364-day paper was assigned at 27.15 pct.</p>
<p>Last week there were 28-day Cetes on offer.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned		Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>27-Day	900 million pesos   2.37 bln pesos     2.63</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.97 bln pesos     4.41</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   2.57 bln pesos     2.86</p>
<p>357-Day     600 million pesos   2.27 bln pesos     3.78</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.38 compared with 3.48 the week before, on demand of 11.50 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails this week were as follows:</p>
<p>    27-Day			   6  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   9  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 15  basis points</p>
<p>    357-Day			 nil basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
</text>
